<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Description</key>
    <string>This import is verified by the signature step of the download recipe (AuthenticodeVerifier on the vendor's installer: a valid, timestamped signature of Grammarly, Inc. under a pinned root), which the packer hands over to the packed EXE that it builds from that installer in the same run, so a real run needs only the dry-run switch of the override. Without that step CimianImporter refuses a real run unless the override sets cimian_allow_unverified to true (the run then publishes with a WARNING, and the report says published, NOT verified). MAIN CAVEAT: Grammarly for Windows installs PER USER, into the profile of the account that runs its installer (the vendor's article; seen on a test PC on 2026-11-13, where the installer run as SYSTEM installed into SYSTEM's own profile), and a per-machine install needs a subscription bought through the vendor's Sales team. A Cimian client runs installers as SYSTEM, so the downloaded installer is NOT published as it is: it is packed into one self-extracting EXE (GrammarlyPerUserPackager, in this folder) that stages the installer under Program Files and registers a scheduled task that runs at the sign-in of any user, as that user, and installs Grammarly into that person's profile when the person has none; the EXE starts the task once for whoever is signed in. So every person who signs in on a PC with this item gets Grammarly (about 85 MB each): it suits PCs of one person, not shared ones. Grammarly then updates itself in each profile, so the item's version is only the version of the staged installer, and the item's install check reads the entry that the EXE writes, not any person's Grammarly. On 2026-11-16 a build of this recipe ran under AutoPkg into a scratch repository, the packed EXE ran as SYSTEM on one Windows 11 test PC with exit code 0, and an on-demand start of the task gave Grammarly to that PC's one signed-in user (an administrator); that was the first build. The current form, which carries the two per-user scripts inside install-machine.ps1, checks the extraction folder and starts the task once itself, also ran there under AutoPkg and as SYSTEM on that PC (exit code 0; its start of the task found Grammarly present), but with it the per-user install path and the removal have not run. NOT established: a real sign-in, a standard user, an upgrade, the item through the Cimian client. Hands the packed EXE that the download recipe built (about 87 MB) to CimianImporter, which publishes it as a new version of the item into a Cimian repository (as a copy of the item's newest pkginfo, with what belongs to the installer file replaced), or says that nothing is new. The version label is the one that the download recipe's WindowsExeVersion step read from the downloaded installer itself (its ProductVersion when that is numbers and dots only, else the four numbers of its fixed file information); the packed EXE carries that installer and keeps its version. The label must equal what a person reads in the installer's properties, which the first dry run shows. CimianImporter does not check that an EXE is the same product as the template (it only compares the upgrade code of an MSI). This is a dry run, which writes nothing, until the recipe's override sets cimian_dry_run to false. The repository is the input cimian_repo or the AutoPkg preference CIMIAN_REPO.</string>
    <key>Identifier</key>
    <string>com.github.serrc-techops.cimian.Grammarly</string>
    <key>Input</key>
    <dict>
        <key>CIMIAN_NAME</key>
        <string>grammarly</string>
        <key>CIMIAN_SUBDIRECTORY</key>
        <string></string>
        <key>NAME</key>
        <string>Grammarly</string>
        <key>pkginfo</key>
        <dict>
            <key>developer</key>
            <string>Grammarly</string>
            <key>display_name</key>
            <string>Grammarly</string>
        </dict>
    </dict>
    <key>MinimumVersion</key>
    <string>1.0.0</string>
    <key>ParentRecipe</key>
    <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.Grammarly-Win</string>
    <key>Process</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>Processor</key>
            <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/CimianImporter</string>
            <key>Arguments</key>
            <dict>
                <key>pathname</key>
                <string>%pathname%</string>
                <key>cimian_name</key>
                <string>%CIMIAN_NAME%</string>
                <key>cimian_subdirectory</key>
                <string>%CIMIAN_SUBDIRECTORY%</string>
                <key>version</key>
                <string>%version%</string>
            </dict>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
